e[28]=slide('Growth arithmetic','Growing history can produce quadratic input volume',code('Assume n calls; initial input B; each call adds d tokens.\nNo pruning, compaction or window cap in this toy model.\n\nInput at call k = B + (k − 1)d\nTotal input     = nB + d × n(n − 1) / 2\n\nB = 5,000; d = 2,000; n = 10\nLast call = 23,000; total input = 140,000 tokens.'),'This is an input-volume model. Apply actual cache, output and tool rates to calculate the bill.','Do not call it a measured session, and do not claim wall time or billed cost must follow the same curve. The expression counts the input to every call under the stated constant-growth assumptions.',tag='Worked arithmetic')
e[33]=slide('Cache break-even','Include the write before counting savings',code('Same eligible prefix; all later requests hit the cache.\nNormalize ordinary input cost to 1 per request.\n\nTotal cached cost = w + (n − 1)r\nCaching saves when w + (n − 1)r < n.\n\nExample r = 0.10:\nw = 1.25 → savings at 2 requests\nw = 2.00 → savings at 3 requests'),'Illustrative multipliers: verify model, platform, TTL and expiry rules. A cache miss changes the calculation.','The examples match common Claude cache-write multipliers, but reads differ across models. Cache entries must exist and remain eligible. With a 0.10 read multiplier, two requests at a double-price write cost 2.10 versus 2.00 uncached, so three are needed. Excludes varying tails, output and tool costs.',theme='dark',tag='Worked arithmetic')
e[47]=slide('Workflow sketch','Make the retry edge explicit',code('PSEUDOCODE — not a harness API\n\nfindings = investigate(rule, calculation, export)\nplan = reconcile(findings, acceptance_cases)\nlatest_failures = []\nfor attempt in range(3):\n    patch = implement(plan, latest_failures)\n    result = run_acceptance_checks(patch)\n    if result.passed: return request_review(patch, result)\n    latest_failures = result.failures\nreturn report_blocked(latest_failures)'),'Use enforced tool, time and cost limits around the workflow. Assign an owner to integration.','A shape to discuss, not runnable Python or a product command. The workflow starts with an empty failure list and known acceptance cases. Passing checks returns a review candidate. Stop if a required permission or missing fact prevents a meaningful next step.',tag='Workflow reference')
